{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01XPAoPoyBKLro5g4ni49VSk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user, single-folder productivity + R&D control system for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (plain markdown as source of truth, no DB, Python stdlib only with one declared `pywinpty` exception).\n\nWhat it is and does:\n\n- **A task/productivity manager.** `anchor_gui.py` is a self-contained stdlib HTTP server (port 8777, run persistently by the NSSM `anchor` service) that renders a browser dashboard and reads/writes markdown directly (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`). Tasks move through a lifecycle â€” active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved-for-later â†’ restored â€” with priority/energy/due/notes fields. `anchor.py` mirrors the same logic as a CLI and emits a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **An R&D \"mission control\" / \"project cockpit\" for trio-driven work.** Layered on top is a control surface for running the **researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman** trio (research Â· plan Â· build) as durable, server-side sessions. Each project gets a window where the three lanes show their most-recent session as a status-lit tile (green/amber/red/grey) that expands an inline panel with a cached summary plus a live terminal.\n\n- **Real interactive terminals with isolation.** It ships ConPTY terminal sessions (via the lone optional `pywinpty` dep) over a hand-rolled stdlib WebSocket / SSE transport to xterm.js, each session running in its own git worktree+branch, with a durable session registry under `.anchor/`. A lane's skill auto-loads and greets exactly once (no repeating-prompt loop), and an engine toggle swaps Claudeâ†”Gemini in place.\n\n- **Supporting machinery it ships:** cached/validated session + project summaries (generate-twice + grounding filter), per-lane doc-role maps, cost/tokens/time rollups, a \"Grass Catchers\" idea board with promote-to-lane, deliverable declare/pin + type-aware launch (skill/tool/service/program/doc), ephemeral deliverable previews hard-guarded off port 8777, stage handoffs between plan and build, and Ghost World Labs branding.\n\n- **Self-verifying.** A 5 AM Windows-scheduled `anchor_healthcheck.py` parses every markdown file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint and the full v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces (all model calls stubbed, never live `claude`), and writes a daily report â€” flagging failures with a red dashboard banner.\n\nThe current state (per CLAUDE.md): the **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** surface was built by Foreman (9 waves green, 637 tests) and merged to master on 2026-06-13."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f293f63b-7eaa-482d-b52e-406553279f33","uuid":"0a8243ce-8043-45a8-9a61-e8ec55decf99","request_id":"req_011Cc1i9X7CVPnU2XVnAxwNa"}
